<http://data.silknow.org/object/a0585671-f5d8-325f-8788-9d1301e4cf68>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Woman's linen smock, 1600s, Spanish; embroidered with pink silk, insertions, lace trim, high neck and collar"@en , "Woman’s smock of bleached linen with a high neck and turn-down collar.  The front and back are 1 rectangle of linen with 2 triangular gores on each side.  The sleeves are rectangular, cartridge-pleated into ⅜-inch (8 mm) wide cuffs; the sleeve gussets are cut diagonally into the body of the smock.  The side and sleeve seams are joined by ¾ inch (1.9 mm) bobbin lace insertions of pink silk and bleached linen thread.  The gore seams and hem are embroidered over with pink silk floss.  Counted-thread stitch embroidery with pink silk floss in a geometric pattern decorates the sleeves and neck opening. The 2-inch (5 cm) deep collar is made of narrow strips of linen joined by a deep bobbin lace insertion of pink silk and bleach linen thread.  The neck opening, collar and cuffs are edged with ½-inch (1.3 cm) bobbin lace, embroidered with pink silk floss. There is a buttonhole worked in pink silk floss at the end of each cuff and the neck fastens with a 1/16-inch (1.5 mm) wide flat braid of pink and white silk floss."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/b3b58e56-8e2d-38ca-9fa9-220de64c62b3> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/d243e3cb-07b9-3268-a2e3-c0b81c906a34> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/3c047bc5-589e-3d0b-82fc-c0dd5d31dfaa> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/6d0ee1e3-2bef-3006-810d-1e8e2a7b1f3c> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/122ff557-ca1e-3922-925a-9cac238f4650> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Woman's linen smock, 1600s, Spanish; embroidered with pink silk, insertions, lace trim, high neck and collar"@en , "Woman’s smock of bleached linen with a high neck and turn-down collar.  The front and back are 1 rectangle of linen with 2 triangular gores on each side.  The sleeves are rectangular, cartridge-pleated into ⅜-inch (8 mm) wide cuffs; the sleeve gussets are cut diagonally into the body of the smock.  The side and sleeve seams are joined by ¾ inch (1.9 mm) bobbin lace insertions of pink silk and bleached linen thread.  The gore seams and hem are embroidered over with pink silk floss.  Counted-thread stitch embroidery with pink silk floss in a geometric pattern decorates the sleeves and neck opening. The 2-inch (5 cm) deep collar is made of narrow strips of linen joined by a deep bobbin lace insertion of pink silk and bleach linen thread.  The neck opening, collar and cuffs are edged with ½-inch (1.3 cm) bobbin lace, embroidered with pink silk floss. There is a buttonhole worked in pink silk floss at the end of each cuff and the neck fastens with a 1/16-inch (1.5 mm) wide flat braid of pink and white silk floss."@en ;
