        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woman’s smock of bleached linen with a high neck and turn-down collar.  The front and back are 1 rectangle of linen with 2 triangular gores on each side.  The sleeves are rectangular, cartridge-pleated into ⅜-inch (8 mm) wide cuffs; the sleeve gussets are cut diagonally into the body of the smock.  The side and sleeve seams are joined by ¾ inch (1.9 mm) bobbin lace insertions of pink silk and bleached linen thread.  The gore seams and hem are embroidered over with pink silk floss.  Counted-thread stitch embroidery with pink silk floss in a geometric pattern decorates the sleeves and neck opening. The 2-inch (5 cm) deep collar is made of narrow strips of linen joined by a deep bobbin lace insertion of pink silk and bleach linen thread.  The neck opening, collar and cuffs are edged with ½-inch (1.3 cm) bobbin lace, embroidered with pink silk floss. There is a buttonhole worked in pink silk floss at the end of each cuff and the neck fastens with a 1/16-inch (1.5 mm) wide flat braid of pink and white silk floss."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/a0585671-f5d8-325f-8788-9d1301e4cf68> .

